d type 2 diabetes who missed several doses of the home blood pressure medicine. Blood pressure was 168/98 at a clinic visit with a mild headache, now resolved. Denies chest pain, vision changes or weakness. Admitted for observation, restarting the medicine, sliding-scale insulin for the glucose, and vitamin B12 for a low level from long-term metformin.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for a mild headache (resolved). Negative for chest pain, shortness of breath, vision change, numbness, weakness, nausea or palpitations.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 98.3 F, HR 78, BP 159/93, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 0/10 | Wt 85 kg, BMI 27.8\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Warm, dry, intact.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: \n\n**Assessment and plan**\n60-year-old male with no significant history admitted with hypertension, follow-up for elevated blood pressure.\n\n**Hypertension, follow-up for elevated blood pressure**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"60-year-old male presenting with elevated blood pressure and mild headache; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Elevated blood pressure and mild headache\n\n**HPI**\n60-year-old male with hypertension and type 2 diabetes who missed several doses of the home blood pressure medicine. Blood pressure was 168/98 at a clinic visit with a mild headache, now resolved. Denies chest pain, vision changes or weakness. Admitted for observation, restarting the medicine, sliding-scale insulin for the glucose, and vitamin B12 for a low level from long-term metformin.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 98.3 F, HR 79, BP 164/98, RR 17, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 0/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Warm, dry, intact.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: pending\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 lisinopril (PRINIVIL,ZESTRIL) 10 mg Oral\n- 0445 insulin lispro (HUMALOG) Per low-dose sliding scale Subcutaneous\n- 0445 cyanocobalamin (VITAMIN B12) 1,000 mcg Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Hypertension, follow-up for elevated blood pressure. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuild